BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Talk w/ GC Myers at West End Gallery
DTSTART:20261107T160000Z
DTEND:20261107T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T153814Z
UID:6972f09cd150e95e2bbe1580328922451be338bc@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art,Connection
DESCRIPTION:Gallery Talk with GC MYERS\nJoin us for this highly anticipate
 d Gallery Talk with GC Myers!\nWhether you're an art collector\, an art ap
 preciator\, a fellow artist\, an aspiring artist\, or simply ‘art-curiou
 s\,’ this is a wonderful opportunity to listen to the Artist speak about
  his newest collection of paintings. During the talk\, Myers may share the
  inspirational story that began his career as a professional artist\, insi
 ght into his creative process\, and a bit of everything in between.\nBONUS
 ! At least one original painting will be given away during a free drawing 
 at the end of the talk. Drawing entries will be permitted until 11:15am fo
 r guests facing unexpected delays. One entry per person is allowed.\nSeati
 ng is limited. Early arrival is suggested to claim a seat. Doors will open
  by 10:30am.\nThe event will take place on the first floor in the Main Gal
 lery which is wheelchair accessible. All events are free and open to the p
 ublic. We hope to see you soon!\nGC Myers' 25th Solo Exhibit\, "The Jubile
 e Dance\," will be on view until Thursday\, November 12th at 5pm.\nENJOY I
 N PERSON: at West End Gallery | 12 West Market Street Corning\, NY. The Ga
 llery is open Tuesday-Saturday from 11am to 5pm.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - 
 https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507606/20261107110000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78507606/20261107110000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CHARM Mural Ribbon Cutting
DTSTART:20261107T170000Z
DTEND:20261107T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T153814Z
UID:651c1b288d39cc284a973bce8d6896131fe96727@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art
DESCRIPTION:Event by Community Arts of Elmira\nCentertown Parking Garage\,
  101 W. Gray Street\, Elmira New York 14901\nDuration: 30 min\nPublic\nShi
 ne or Rain! Public Art Mural Ribbon Cutting!\nCommunity Arts of Elmira "El
 mira Infinite Canvas" Presents:\nCelebrating "Curtain Call: Soul of the St
 age" Designed by Artist Dion Browne of Dion designs / DesignerWear\, and i
 nstalled by Dion and collaborating Artist Sam Somostrada of SOMO Art!\nThi
 s mural was inspired by the history of theatre and the performing arts in 
 Elmira\, New York\, on the Centertown Parking Garage\, Elmira\, NY\, 101 W
 . Gray Street\, Elmira\, New York\, 14901\, and is located on the southeas
 t tower on lower Railroad Avenue\, across the entrance to the Clemens Perf
 orming Arts Center\, celebrating 50 years in 2027!\nCommunity Arts of Elmi
 ra "Elmira Infinite Canvas" public art program is grateful to work with su
 ch superlatives as Artist Dion Browne\, Artist Sam Somostrada (Todd Omos)
 \, the Clemens Center\, City of Elmira\, The ARTS Council of the Southern 
 Finger Lakes and New York State Council on the Arts!\nCultivating Havens f
 or the Arts through Regional Murals (CHARM) is a Governor’s Initiative e
 stablished by Governor Hochul in 2025 and administered by the New York Sta
 te Council on the Arts (NYSCA).\nThis mural is made possible by the New Yo
 rk State Council on the Arts CHARM Initiative with support from the Office
  of the Governor and is administered locally by The ARTS Council of the So
 uthern Finger Lakes in partnership with Community Arts of Elmira.\nThe mis
 sion of the New York State Council on the Arts (NYSCA) is to foster and ad
 vance the full breadth of New York State’s arts\, culture\, and creativi
 ty for all. Annually\, NYSCA funding supports over 3\,000 artists and arts
  and culture organizations across all 10 state regions. In FY2027\, NYSCA 
 will award more than $161 million. Created in 1960 and continued with the 
 support of Governor Kathy Hochul and the New York State Legislature\, NYSC
 A is a state agency part of the Executive Branch.\n#community #collaborati
 on #partnership #together\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.l
 y/o9b0uzpj/event/78508386/20261107120000
GEO:42.09354;-76.804137
LOCATION:Community Arts of Elmira\, 413 Lake Street\, Elmira\, New York\, 
 14901\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78508386/20261107120000
END:VEVENT
